docs {
  # List Eligible Participants

  - **Method** `GET`
  - **Endpoint** `/api/v1/groups/:groupID/expenses/participants`
  - **Auth** Bearer access token

  ## Description

  Lists current and former group memberships available for expense shares. Copy `member_id` into `shares[].member_id`. The same user can have different membership IDs in different groups. Inactive memberships and records with a departure date stay selectable. The endpoint includes profiles and available avatar URLs.

  An active account and active membership with no departure timestamp are required. A site admin also needs active membership. Example IDs are illustrative. Use IDs from your own group. Reads are available in `ACTIVE`, `SETTLING` and `CLOSED`.

  ## Enum values

  | Field | Values | Meaning |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | `status` | `ACTIVE`, `INACTIVE` | Membership status. Eligibility here includes both. |
  | `group status` | `ACTIVE`, `SETTLING`, `CLOSED` | All three allow reads. |

  ## Request

  ### Headers
  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `Authorization` | `string` | Yes | Bearer access token (`Bearer <token>`). |

  ### Path parameters
  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `groupID` | `integer` | Yes | Positive signed 64-bit group ID. Bruno variable `expenseGroupId`. |

  ### Query parameters
  | Field | Type | Required | Description |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | `page` | `integer` | No | Defaults to 1. Minimum 1. |
  | `limit` | `integer` | No | Defaults to 20. Range 1 to 100. |

  Omitted or empty page and limit use their defaults. Explicit zero, negatives, non-integers, limits above 100 and overflowing offsets return `BAD_REQUEST`. Sorted by member_id ascending.

  ### Body
  Send this request without a body.

  ## Response

  **`200 OK`**

  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "data": {
      "items": [
        {
          "member_id": 30,
          "user_id": 130,
          "name": "Ali",
          "avatar_attachment_id": null,
          "avatar_url": null,
          "status": "ACTIVE",
          "joined_at": "2026-11-17T08:00:00Z",
          "left_at": null
        },
        {
          "member_id": 31,
          "user_id": 131,
          "name": "Reza",
          "avatar_attachment_id": 501,
          "avatar_url": null,
          "status": "INACTIVE",
          "joined_at": "2026-11-17T08:30:00Z",
          "left_at": "2026-11-20T09:00:00Z"
        }
      ],
      "pagination": {
        "page": 1,
        "limit": 20,
        "total": 2
      }
    }
  }
  ```

  ### Response fields

  | Field | Type | Meaning |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | `items` | `array` | Memberships on the requested page. |
  | `items[].member_id` | `integer` | ID to submit in a share. |
  | `items[].user_id` | `integer` | Global user ID for user profile operations. |
  | `items[].name` | `string` | Display name, or an empty string when unavailable. |
  | `items[].avatar_attachment_id` | `integer \| null` | Avatar record ID when present. |
  | `items[].avatar_url` | `string \| null` | Signed avatar URL if accessible. |
  | `items[].status` | `string` | ACTIVE or INACTIVE. |
  | `items[].joined_at` | `RFC 3339 timestamp` | Membership join date. |
  | `items[].left_at` | `RFC 3339 timestamp \| null` | Recorded departure time. |
  | `pagination.page` | `integer` | Effective page number. |
  | `pagination.limit` | `integer` | Effective page size. |
  | `pagination.total` | `integer` | Count before slicing, after any filters and access rules. An out-of-range page still returns this count. |

  ### Empty page

  ```json
  {
    "success": true,
    "data": {
      "items": [],
      "pagination": {
        "page": 2,
        "limit": 20,
        "total": 2
      }
    }
  }
  ```

  ## Errors

  | HTTP | code | error | When it happens |
  | --- | --- | --- | --- |
  | 400 | `BAD_REQUEST` | `bad request payload or parameters` | Invalid group ID or pagination. |
  | 401 | `MISSING_TOKEN` | `authorization token is missing` | Missing Authorization header or invalid Bearer header format. |
  | 401 | `TOKEN_INVALID` | `authorization token is invalid` | Invalid access token, including use of a refresh token in its place. |
  | 401 | `TOKEN_EXPIRED` | `authorization token has expired` | Access token expired. Refresh it or sign in again. |
  | 401 | `TOKEN_REVOKED` | `authorization token has been revoked` | Access token is blacklisted. |
  | 403 | `USER_INACTIVE` | `user account is deactivated` | Caller account is inactive. |
  | 403 | `EXPENSE_FORBIDDEN` | `only active group members can access expenses` | The caller lacks active membership in the group. |
  | 404 | `USER_NOT_FOUND` | `user not found` | Caller account is missing or soft-deleted. |
  | 404 | `GROUP_NOT_FOUND` | `group not found` | Group is missing or soft-deleted. |
  | 500 | `INTERNAL_SERVER_ERROR` | `an internal server error occurred` | Database, transaction or token verification dependency failed. |
  | 503 | `STORAGE_UNAVAILABLE` | `storage service is temporarily unavailable` | Required attachment URL signing failed. |

  ### `403 EXPENSE_FORBIDDEN` example

  ```json
  {
    "success": false,
    "code": "EXPENSE_FORBIDDEN",
    "error": "only active group members can access expenses"
  }
  ```
}
